          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "I grew up in Golden, Colorado, and spent my twenties drawing buildings for an architecture firm in Chicago. Photography started as a way to remember the places I was drawing. It became the work when I realised I cared more about how light moved across a wall than about the wall itself."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Since 2016 I have photographed mountains, coastlines and modernist buildings for publishers, architects and a handful of hotels. I shoot slowly, mostly on a large-format camera, and print every edition by hand in my studio in RiNo."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "column": 1,
          "variant": "default"
        },
